WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.400
On the fifteenth of November a fleet of computers asked one hundred and twenty questions of a game's brain.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.200
One passed.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.400
It took three hours and six minutes and forty-four jobs to be believed.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.800
The same evening, the cards trained a net that passed every test but the last one.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.600
They have run two hundred and six hours since, and kept nothing.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.800
The Orrery Q process.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.000
A fleet, two learners and a warm room, traced from the outside in.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.400
Part one.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.200
The whole.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.800
An orrery is a clockwork model of the solar system:

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.000
one sun, every planet on its own arm.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.800
This fleet is built the same way.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.800
One Mac asks every question.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.400
Housekeeping turns on the inner orbit, every few minutes.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.800
The CPU lanes on the middle one, a job of minutes.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.800
The cards on the outer, half an hour or more.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.000
Every arrow is one connection from the Mac.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.000
No machine speaks to another.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.800
What the orrery turns is two learning loops.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.600
On the left, the game's hand-written brain:

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:28.000
a dial is moved, read on seeds, read again on seeds it was never chosen on, and proved against what stands.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:36.400
On the right, a population of nets evolves on each card, is examined against a ladder of old champions, and elected.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.000
Between them, the bridge:

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.800
a net the game accepts becomes a style the left loop plays.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.000
Strip the tanks away and this is anyone's problem.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.800
A trial is one setting to try.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:57.400
A seed is one example, a game whose dice are fixed by a number.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.200
A held-out read is the validation set.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.200
The proof is the final test against what is deployed.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:10.200
An island is one training run, a milestone a checkpoint, the bridge the deployment test.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.400
The application, as components.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.200
The window, forty-six thousand lines of Rust with no libraries, only reads.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.400
The keeper runs a thread a lane and reaches each machine by ssh.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.200
The planner decides what to ask next and what an answer means.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.000
Everything is a file in one folder:

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:32.800
the queue.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.200
And the hearth reads the room and sets the fleet's watts.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.600
Part two.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.600
The window, page by page.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.800
The Queue's Fleet page:

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.400
the scheduler's live view.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.800
Sixty-five thousand six hundred jobs done since the twenty-eighth of October.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.800
Four hundred and sixty-three failed:

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.400
seven in a thousand.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.600
The newest read:

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.800
a guess inside its error, as most are.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.000
The room's line:

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
twenty-six point four degrees, a hundred and seventy watts short.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.200
And a machine:

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.200
its load, its temperatures against their limits, and its buttons.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.800
The Timeline is a Gantt chart of the whole fleet.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:23.000
Every lane is a row; every job a block coloured by its stage:

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.600
blue a first read, green a read-on, coral a held-out read, pink a proof.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.600
The strip at the foot is the Mac itself, planning.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.000
Blame answers the question every operator asks:

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.600
why is this waiting?

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.600
Its verdict at five o'clock:

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.600
no machine waits on another.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:53.600
A trial's step waits one point two minutes for the planner and one point four in the queue, for four point six minutes of work.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:01.800
The Lineup puts every chain of work in its own row, and judges it.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.200
Amber:

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.000
still going.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:03.800
Red walls:

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.000
dead ends, dropped after one read, or four.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.600
On this page, one hundred and thirty-one dead ends.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.600
The Hit Parade is the scoreboard.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:24.000
Today, one thousand six hundred and forty-eight jobs done; ninety-eight percent came back done; ninety-eight an hour; fifteen point seven kilowatt-hours.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.000
And a bar a day since the twenty-eighth of October.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.400
Part three.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.200
One investigation:

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.600
a CPU generation, and a GPU generation, followed to the end.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.200
The trial moved one dial:

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:48.000
the order in which a tank takes its ladder of jobs, from as built to expand first.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.800
It had been asked thirty-eight times before.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:58.000
Twice it passed, and twice one regression family stopped it, at seventy-nine percent against a floor of eighty.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.200
On the thirteenth, the game gained a rule:

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.400
a small drop passes and moves its floor.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:10.400
On the fifteenth the family read seventy-nine point six, and the rule let it through.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.000
How are examples kept apart?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.200
Each kind of read draws its seeds from its own block of numbers.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.000
The first read from twenty million up.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Read-ons from three hundred million.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Held-out reads from sixty million, a block no trial touches.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.400
The proof from seven hundred million.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.000
Any machine given a block plays the same games.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.600
Orrery draws the chain itself.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.400
Following w21532:

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.800
twenty jobs on six machines, framed in amber, each arrow the order one followed the last.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.000
The green rules:

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.600
the promotion, and main.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.200
Every job on one clock.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.800
Thin bars wait for a lane; thick bars run.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.200
The first read and three read-ons:

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:05.800
past the bar at five hundred and ten seeds, z two point nine two.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.200
One read-on was asked twice, by a race in the planner:

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.600
ten minutes on the slowest machine.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.000
Three held-out reads on fresh seeds:

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.400
pooled z three point one three.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.200
Then three rounds of proof against main:

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:25.000
plus zero point five nine a seat, z four point two seven.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.000
Fifty minutes running, forty-three waiting for a lane, eighty-one proving.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.800
What happened to the other hundred and nineteen?

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.000
Twenty-one played the very games of the defaults:

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.000
the change was never reached.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.600
Lucky first reads regressed.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.200
A map vetoed one.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.000
A sequential pass failed on fresh seeds.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.200
On the cards:

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:56.400
fourteen segments in the window, four that could not be elected, three that held, one forced in, and none taken by the game.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.400
The same evening on boburner's card.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.400
Four hours in the queue:

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.800
each island keeps six segments waiting.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:10.200
Forty-nine minutes, a hundred generations of two thousand and forty-eight nets.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.800
Every floor held, z plus one point nine nine against a bar of three.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.000
Elected because three hours had passed without one.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:27.800
Forty-nine minutes later the game read it eight point eight four a seat worse than the net it ships, and refused it.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.800
The election did one more thing:

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.000
it raised every floor to M0049's own share.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.000
When the game refused M0049, the top rung went back.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.600
The floors did not.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.800
The standing top scores zero point seven eight five on take and hold.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.400
The floor is now zero point nine one eight.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:56.800
Three hundred and sixteen segments, two hundred and six GPU-hours since, and none has met them.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.800
Now the net itself, outside in.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:02.600
The tank:

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:06.200
twelve rays every thirty degrees, each read three ways:

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.000
the nearest thing, the enemy, a pillbox.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.600
The input sensor matrix:

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:18.600
those thirty-six, then the body, the rules' own answer, the gun, the route, the arcs and two cells of memory.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.400
Sixty-four numbers.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.200
The transform:

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.800
two layers of forty-eight.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:26.200
Ninety-six percent of their values sit at plus or minus one.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.600
It is a net of switches.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:29.800
The output matrix:

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.600
six numbers.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.800
And the gate.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.400
One neuron opens it.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:37.400
Open, the tank adds the net's corrections to the rules.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.800
Shut, it plays the rules exactly.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:44.200
It is open on less than seven steps in a hundred.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.400
What does it use?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:54.400
Hold each group of senses at its average and see how far the outputs move.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.600
The rules' own answer, the near rays and its own body matter most.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.600
The route, the sense added for the mazes, matters least.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.000
Its weights are no bigger than mutation alone would make them.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.200
Is it getting better?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.800
Two fixed yardsticks say.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:14.600
The brain:

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:23.400
eight point two two points a seat over main of the twenty-eighth of October, on the same two thousand seeds every day.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.800
Four of it in five days.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.600
Then flat.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.400
The nets:

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:31.800
a gauntlet share from sixty-four to eighty percent in two days.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.400
Then flat for eleven.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.600
The game has taken nothing since the tenth.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.000
Part four.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.800
The watts, and the room they heat.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:49.800
With the flat's own heating off, the fleet is the heating.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:56.200
The room has stayed within half a degree of eighty Fahrenheit for most of two days.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.600
Full tilt sheds nothing, by design:

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:01.000
it took the room to eighty-two.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:07.400
And since noon today the fleet gives four hundred and fifty watts, and the room slides.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.800
Everything here heats like a small room:

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:18.800
its time constant is how many degrees a watt, times how many joules a degree.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:19.600
boburner's card:

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.000
zero point three five times two hundred and thirteen, seventy-five seconds.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:24.800
whitewolf's card:

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:25.600
six minutes.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:26.400
The room:

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:32.000
four point two megajoules a degree, over a hundred and twenty watts a degree:

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.600
nine point seven hours.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.600
That is why the controller waits forty minutes between changes.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.600
The budget at sixteen thirty-one today.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:50.200
The room at twenty-six point three five, the target twenty-six point seven, falling twelve hundredths a degree an hour.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:51.400
The distance term:

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.200
forty-two watts.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.400
The falling term:

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.000
a hundred and forty.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:55.800
The budget:

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.800
one hundred and eighty-two watts.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:03.000
Most of it is where the room is heading, not where it is.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.800
Two hundred and seventeen megajoules in seventy-four hours:

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.800
sixty kilowatt-hours, about ten dollars.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.800
And what each joule bought:

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.800
columbia does a job for four watt-hours; bosporus for forty-eight.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.800
That is why the hold sheds the old servers first.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.800
Two faults were found by looking.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:35.000
The room controller woke calber every forty minutes; calber never answered, and the three lanes the controller had paused itself waited behind it.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.800
Now a machine that does not answer is left for three hours.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:44.200
At twelve minutes past five, whitewolf's card went back to work.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:48.600
And the telemetry fetched every older day again every five minutes:

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:53.000
fourteen point nine gigabytes, of which point one four is real.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.600
The fetch is fixed.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:57.400
Removing the copies waits for a person.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.200
What went well.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.400
Sixty-five thousand jobs, seven in a thousand failed.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.400
The brain eight points a seat better on fixed seeds.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:12.400
A proof that refused a generation that did not repeat.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.600
A room held by the fleet's own heat.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:17.200
Where to step in.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:17.600
First:

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.600
when the game refuses a net, put the floors back.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:22.000
Second:

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.200
let the game's verdict weigh in the election.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:25.600
Third:

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:31.200
give the brain something new to search; the keeper says it needs a change.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:40.000
Then the race that asked a read twice, a proof sized by each machine's speed, and a GPU queue sized in minutes.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:50.600
A change is believed only on seeds it was not chosen on, and kept only if it beats what stands.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.000
The centre asks; the planets answer.
